accTitle: Keep one client resolver and split queries by namespace
accDescr: EC2 uses AmazonProvidedDNS. A domain-specific forward rule sends AD queries through an outbound endpoint to directory DNS, while AWS private names resolve in the VPC.
C[EC2 client]:::inputData --> R[AmazonProvidedDNS]:::decision
R --> Q{private.example.com<br/>namespace?}:::decision
Q -->|Yes| F[Associated FORWARD rule<br/>Outbound Resolver endpoint]:::decision
F --> A[Managed AD DNS servers<br/>Two target IPs]:::output
Q -->|No, Kinesis private name| K[Private DNS resolution<br/>Interface endpoint IPs]:::output
